===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)kewh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|schewen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|scēawian||to look, look at, exhibit, display}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skauwōn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skawwōną|t=to look, see}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)kewh₁-||to heed, look, feel, take note of}}; see {{m|en|haw}}, {{m|en|gaum}}, {{m|en|caveat}}, {{m|en|caution}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|shaw||to show}}, {{cog|nl|schouwen||to inspect, view}}, {{cog|de|schauen||to see, behold}}, {{cog|da|skue||to behold}}. Related to {{l|en|sheen}}.

Wider cognates include {{cog|grc|κῦδος}}, {{cog|la|caveō}} whence {{cog|en|caution}} and {{m|en|caveat}},  and {{cog|sa|कवि|tr=kaví||seer, prophet, bard}}.

